cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GenIaC-SecBench in your research, please cite the paper below."
title: "GenIaC-SecBench: A Human-Anchored Security Benchmark for LLM-Generated Infrastructure-as-Code"
abstract: >-
  GenIaC-SecBench evaluates the security posture of LLM-generated
  Infrastructure-as-Code against a size-matched human baseline. It comprises 100
  deployment scenarios stratified by architectural complexity, 1,196 generated
  artifacts across 12 model configurations from four vendors, complete scan
  coverage by three independent policy engines (Checkov, Trivy, KICS), and 634
  human-authored IaC templates scanned with the identical toolchain to provide
  the reference point that model-only benchmarks lack.
